    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0156" n="990" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg990"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 658.119/561</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-12T19:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 12, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10.10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1024. War Trade Board [from Sheldon]:</p>
                <p>No. 1217. Department’s 687, your 1012, August 9, 9 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >4</hi>] p.m. We assume ship is <hi rendition="#italic">Helios</hi>. It will
                    only be necessary to issue United <pb facs="0157" n="991" xml:id="pg991"/>
                    States export license covering cargo, as Contraband Committee has cabled British
                    Consul, Buenos Aires, <hi rendition="#italic">re</hi> the lots approved and
                    Consul will have certified manifest. Swedish Legation informed of numbers
                    through mistake. In future cases export applications for shipment from Buenos
                    Aires, Santos, Montevideo, Rio de Janeiro, Bahia, for Sweden will be submitted
                    to Contraband Committee through newly established Swedish trade office in
                    London. The Contraband Committee’s approval will be cabled to British consul at
                    port of shipment, who will certify to correctness of manifest. I suggest that
                    similar certificates might be required from American consuls.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
